{
  "summary": "P1 security. Reported by Priya Nair (IT Manager, priya.nair@brightline.example): she is seeing failed-login alerts on former employee Ryan Brooks' account (ryan.brooks@brightline.example, user_id 10, ex-Sales AE, left spring 2026). Checked (read-only only): account status = disabled, BUT sign_in_blocked = false and vpn_access = true. Looks like offboarding was not finished. Sign-in logs: 2 failed_password attempts on VPN, 2026-10-09 07:05 and 07:07 UTC (03:05/03:07 ET, overnight), from IP 192.0.2.140, Amsterdam NL, hosting network, no MFA. Looks like credential stuffing or use of stolen credentials against the leftover VPN access. No successful sign-ins in the 14-day window. Nothing was actioned by Tier 1: no block, reset, or unlock, because it's not the sender's account (KB-005). Still needed: security review; block sign-in and revoke VPN for user_id 10; confirm offboarding is complete (device BL-LT-0110, mailbox retention); consider blocking IP 192.0.2.140 and checking other accounts for attempts from it.",
  "reason": "KB-005 says always escalate; P1 security; failed attempts from hosting network on a disabled account that still has VPN access"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Priya, thanks for flagging this. Ryan's account is disabled. But we found two failed VPN sign-in attempts on it early Friday morning (around 3 AM Eastern) from a hosting network in Amsterdam, with no MFA. Neither attempt got in. We also noticed his account still has VPN access and sign-in hasn't been fully blocked, so his offboarding looks unfinished. I've passed this to our Tier 2 security team as a high priority. They'll review the attempts and lock down the remaining access. We didn't change anything on his account from our side. Tier 2 will follow up with you.",
  "internal_note": "Sender: Priya Nair (IT Manager, user_id 3), verified sender email. Subject account: Ryan Brooks (user_id 10), status disabled, but sign_in_blocked=false and vpn_access=true (offboarding incomplete). Sign-in logs: 2 failed_password attempts on VPN, 2026-10-09 07:05/07:07 UTC (03:05/03:07 ET), IP 192.0.2.140, Amsterdam NL, hosting network, no MFA. No successful sign-ins. Per KB-005 and the own-account rule, Tier 1 only ran read-only checks. No block, reset, or unlock was requested. Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation id 1). Recommended: block sign-in and revoke VPN for user_id 10, complete offboarding (device BL-LT-0110), consider blocking the IP and checking other accounts for attempts from it.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-005"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
